// Failed logon summary
//
// What it looks for: Windows Event ID 4625 ("an account failed to log on"),
// counted per account-and-host pair.
//
// Why it matters: a burst of failed logons is the classic signature of brute
// force or password spraying. Grouping by account AND host is what separates
// them — many failures against one account is brute force, few failures across
// many accounts is spraying. Spraying is the one that stays under lockout
// thresholds, so it's easy to miss if you only count per account.
//
// What a hit means: an account crossing four figures is not a user mistyping a
// password. Pivot next to 4624 for the same account to check whether anything
// eventually succeeded.

SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| summarize FailedAttempts = count() by Account, Computer
| sort by FailedAttempts desc
